# Build the human face: rendered markdown, same Worker

## Step

Apply the [research asset](./research-sveltekit-shell-asset.svx): turn `apps/mischief` into the SvelteKit app that hosts the Effect router, with the agent surfaces byte-for-byte unchanged (the existing route and MCP tests keep passing), and the `text/html` face rendered from the same generated content: home page is the catalogue, `/skills/<name>` pages, light theme, Dank Mono self-hosted, prose styles for rendered markdown, the OG tags. Dependencies pinned exactly, `minimumReleaseAgeExclude` entries where prerelease, the fence extended to `.svelte` per the asset. `alchemy dev` serves both faces locally. Joel signs off on the dependency additions and the first deploy that ships the font files.

Resolved when the gate is green, `curl -H 'Accept: text/html' http://localhost:1337/` returns a SvelteKit-rendered page with the catalogue as real markup, and every existing agent test passes unchanged.

## Result

Resolved on 2026-09-22 with a plain HTML shell on the existing Effect Worker. The SvelteKit implementation was built and passed locally, then deliberately removed after production exposed more adapter cost than product value.

### What shipped

- `apps/mischief/src/html.ts` renders complete static HTML documents for `/`, `/skills`, and known `/skills/<name>` pages.
- `apps/mischief/src/app.ts` negotiates those documents only when `Accept` permits `text/html`; default and agent requests still receive the exact generated Markdown.
- The HTML uses browser-default semantic elements. There is no CSS, font, logo, favicon, OG image, image metadata, or Worker asset binding.
- The generated Markdown renderer still runs at build time against checked-in source. The Worker performs no repository reads and ships no application JavaScript.
- MCP, HTTP, OpenAPI, rate limits, Dynamic Worker execution, discovery documents, DNS-AID, DNSSEC, and auth behavior remain on the original Effect route graph.

### Why SvelteKit was removed

The local SvelteKit implementation needed a TypeScript 7 config-API patch because Kit next.27 expected the removed classic TypeScript compiler API. The first production build then failed because Alchemy beta.79's pinned adapter called Kit 3's removed `generateManifest` API. A second compatibility patch built and deployed the Website, but live MCP requests threw Cloudflare 1101 while HTML and static routes returned 200. The launch smoke caught the broken behavior immediately.

Joel: "plain html 86 sveltkit wanking".

The deployment was first restored to the previous Effect Worker, which returned MCP to green. SvelteKit, `@alchemy.run/frontend-frameworks`, `@rsvelte/svelte-check`, Vite app configuration, Svelte components, route loaders, generated Kit state, and both compatibility patches were then removed. The final plain HTML Worker replaced the restored version.

### Verification

- `pnpm turbo run check test build`: 20/20 tasks passed on a cold local Turbo cache.
- `pnpm lint`: passed.
- `git diff --check`: passed.
- Mischief: 13/13 tests passed, including HTML negotiation for all three human route shapes and exact Markdown discovery bytes.
- Fresh local `alchemy dev --stage mischief-plain-html-dev`: one Worker plus the four existing bindings became ready.
- Final production deploy: one Worker update; zone, DNS-AID, DNSSEC, rate-limit bindings, and WorkerLoader binding were no-ops.
- `pnpm mischief:smoke`: all five routes returned 200, MCP listed `search`, `read`, and `execute`, and isitagentready returned 5/5 Agent-Native.
- Live HTML returned the expected titles for `/`, `/skills`, and `/skills/learn-rat-stack`; raw `/` still began with `# ratstack.sh`.
- Live responses contain no style element, stylesheet link, image element, or image metadata. Former CSS, image, favicon, and font URLs return 404.
- Live MCP `server/discover` advertised only `2026-07-28`.
- Browser inspection showed the full semantic catalogue and navigation.
